  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "What is the value of \\[(2^0-1+5^2+0)^{-1}\\times 5?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-125\\)",
    "B": "\\(-120\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\)",
    "E": "\\(25\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Evaluate the quantity inside parentheses first. Since \\(2\\ne0\\), the zero-exponent rule gives \\(2^0=1\\), and \\(5^2=25\\). Therefore\n\\[\n2^0-1+5^2+0=1-1+25+0=25.\n\\]\nAn exponent of \\(-1\\) means taking the reciprocal of a nonzero number. Thus the requested value is\n\\[\n25^{-1}\\cdot5=\\frac1{25}\\cdot5\n=\\boxed{\\frac15},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
